      "title": "Deckers' Q2 Earnings Beat Estimates on Margins, Revenues Miss",
      "summary": "Deckers Outdoor (DECK) reported Q2 adjusted EPS of $2.03, beating estimates by 11.5%, but sales of $1.48 billion missed forecasts. The company expanded gross margins to 60.5% through tariff refunds and full-price selling, though domestic DTC sales weakened. DECK lowered its fiscal 2027 revenue guidance to $5.70-$5.725 billion while raising EPS guidance to $7.80-$7.95, citing softer consumer demand and reduced growth expectations for both HOKA and UGG brands.",
